    {
      "id": "claim_e84e7ce946194531849290ac6587d399",
      "statement": "itest-run.sh exercises one action per execution scope against the kind/localstack environment (a kube-api `get` on kube-system pods and an aws-api `aws-get` sweep of EC2/Route53 resources), polling GET /runs/{id} until each reports status: succeeded, and also submits an invalid-param request asserting the execution fails to confirm input validation survives the full HTTP path; five aws-get resources requiring LocalStack Pro are not covered by this harness and are instead covered only by unit tests against fakes in internal/actions.",
