      "statement": "The mock-backplane server distinguishes a modeled-but-absent fixture resource (HTTP 501) from a resource that exists but was never granted to the requesting trusted action (HTTP 403), so a gap in fixture coverage cannot be mistaken for a legitimate not-found or a passing negative test; kubectl cannot be used directly against the mock because it does not model Kubernetes API discovery endpoints.",
