      "id": "claim_39ae2624886b49789e4adf65bf0ee924",
      "statement": "components/trusted-actions/tests/proxy-backplane/ is a recording/replay-style reverse proxy used by integration tests to reach a real Kubernetes API: it accepts a base64-encoded kubeconfig at registration (POST /backplane/trustedactions/{clusterId}), builds an http.Transport from its TLS credentials, and forwards arbitrary HTTP methods on the returned proxyUri to the live upstream cluster (injecting the kubeconfig's bearer token) until the registered entry is deleted; it runs via `make proxy-backplane` on PROXY_BACKPLANE_PORT (default 8088).",
